---
import { buildStats, CHASSIS, defaultLoadout, PARTS } from "@void-drift/mode-a";
import LabLayout from "../../layouts/LabLayout.astro";

const chassisIds = ["scout", "wasp", "fighter", "corvette", "fiddler"] as const;
const engines = ["ion", "heavy-ion", "fusion", "plasma"] as const;
const hullBases = chassisIds.map((id) => ({
	name: id[0].toUpperCase() + id.slice(1),
	base: CHASSIS[id].baseSpeed,
}));
const contributions = engines.map((id) => ({
	name: PARTS[id].name,
	contribution: PARTS[id].speedContribution,
}));
const examples = chassisIds.map((chassis) => {
	const build = defaultLoadout(chassis);
	build.side = "ion";
	build.aft = build.aft.map(() => "ion");
	const light = buildStats(build);
	build.side = "fusion";
	build.aft = build.aft.map(() => "fusion");
	const fission = buildStats(build);
	return {
		chassis,
		count: light.engineBreakdown.reduce((n, item) => n + item.count, 0),
		light: light.poweredCruiseCeiling,
		fission: fission.poweredCruiseCeiling,
	};
});
const mixed = defaultLoadout("fighter");
mixed.side = "heavy-ion";
mixed.aft = ["fusion", "plasma"];
const mixedStats = buildStats(mixed);
const mixedParts = mixedStats.engineBreakdown
	.map(
		(entry) =>
			`${entry.count} ${PARTS[entry.id].name}: +${entry.contribution} u/s`,
	)
	.join(" · ");
---

<LabLayout title="Ship propulsion">
	<article class="reference">
		<p class="eyebrow">PRODUCTION RULE / ASSEMBLED FLIGHT</p>
		<h1>Powered cruise ceiling</h1>
		<p class="lead">
			The ceiling is the speed propulsion approaches. It is not a cap on
			coasting or gravity-assisted velocity. Releasing controls does not change
			it, and there is no temporary boost state.
		</p>

		<section>
			<h2>One installed-build value</h2>
			<p>
				<code
					>V = hull base speed + sum of installed main-engine speed
					contributions</code
				>
			</p>
			<p>
				Each physical main engine contributes a fixed scalar. Its angle, thrust
				strength, pulse timing, charge, linkage and power state do not change V.
				Fitted inactive engines still count. Empty slots, equipment and
				stabilizers contribute zero.
			</p>
			<div class="tables">
				<table>
					<caption>
						Hull base speed
					</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Hull</th>
							<th>Base (u/s)</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{hullBases.map(({ name, base }) => (
							<tr>
								<td>{name}</td>
								<td>{base}</td>
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<table>
					<caption>
						Contribution per installed engine
					</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Engine</th>
							<th>Contribution (u/s)</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{contributions.map(({ name, contribution }) => (
							<tr>
								<td>{name}</td>
								<td>{contribution}</td>
							</tr>
						))}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				The Wasp has one centre main engine. Every other hull has two side
				mains; fitted aft engines also count. Fiddler's required rear pair is
				included.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Maximum occupied engine complements</h2>
			<p>
				These values are calculated from valid loadouts and the same definitions
				used by the builder and flight.
			</p>
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Hull</th>
						<th>Engine count</th>
						<th>All Light ion</th>
						<th>All Fission</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{examples.map((row) => (
						<tr>
							<td>{row.chassis[0].toUpperCase() + row.chassis.slice(1)}</td>
							<td>{row.count}</td>
							<td>{row.light} u/s</td>
							<td>{row.fission} u/s</td>
						</tr>
					))}
				</tbody>
			</table>
			<p>
				Worked mixed build — Fighter: {PARTS["heavy-ion"].name} side pair and
				one Fission plus one Plasma aft engine. {mixedParts}. V =
				{mixedStats.hullBaseSpeed}
				+ {mixedStats.installedEngineContribution} =
				<strong>{mixedStats.poweredCruiseCeiling} u/s</strong>. Releasing either
				control changes thrust delivery, not V.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>How forward thrust fades</h2>
			<p>
				For straight forward thrust below V, acceleration follows
				<code>a = a0 × max(0, 1 − speed / V)</code>, where a0 is the available
				forward acceleration at rest. Remaining forward thrust is:
			</p>
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Speed</th>
						<th>Remaining forward thrust</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td>0% of V</td>
						<td>100%</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td>50% of V</td>
						<td>50%</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td>90% of V</td>
						<td>10%</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td>100% of V</td>
						<td>0%</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
			<p>
				With constant forward acceleration a0, from rest, no gravity, and
				continuous engine delivery, the analytical reference is
				<code>v(t) = V × (1 − exp(−a0 × t / V))</code>;
				<code>t95 = −ln(0.05) × V / a0</code>. Fixed-step flight approaches this
				curve within numerical tolerance. Pulse, charge, variable power and
				turning do not meet those assumptions.
			</p>
			<p>
				Braking and transverse steering remain available. Existing speed above V
				is retained; propulsion does not clip it back. Gravity can add
				overspeed. Stabilizers do not affect V.
			</p>
		</section>

		<nav aria-label="Related references">
			<h2>Related references</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<a href="/hangar">Ship builder</a>
					· <a href="/lab/builder">Lab builder</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="/lab/instrument">Motion instrument</a>
					· <a href="/lab/gravity-tuning">Gravity tuning</a>
				</li>
				<li>
					<a href="/lab/studies/ship-motion-laws-2026-11-04"
						>Historical motion study</a
					>
					(its old ceiling comparisons are not current flight evidence)
				</li>
			</ul>
		</nav>
		<p>
			Engine balance remains open for later work. Human handling review is still
			needed, including angled-engine ships and the LHI Wasp and Fiddler.
		</p>
	</article>
</LabLayout>

<style>
.reference {
	max-width: 980px;
	margin: 0 auto;
	color: var(--color-text);
	line-height: 1.65;
}
.eyebrow {
	color: var(--color-text-muted);
	font-size: 0.8rem;
	letter-spacing: 0.12em;
}
h1 {
	font-size: 2.5rem;
	line-height: 1.1;
	margin: 0.3em 0;
}
h2 {
	font-size: 1.5rem;
	line-height: 1.2;
	margin-top: 2rem;
}
.lead {
	font-size: 1.15rem;
	max-width: 72ch;
}
.tables {
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
	gap: 1rem;
}
table {
	width: 100%;
	border-collapse: collapse;
	margin: 1rem 0;
}
caption {
	text-align: left;
	font-weight: 700;
	padding: 0.5rem;
}
th,
td {
	text-align: left;
	padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
	border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
}
th {
	color: var(--color-text-muted);
}
code {
	color: var(--color-selected);
}
nav ul {
	padding-left: 1.3rem;
}
</style>
